|---|---|---|---|
| `sample_ct.nrrd` | CT chest sample volume (`CT-chest.nrrd`, Medical Decathlon test data) | 3D Slicer testing-data mirror, `Slicer/SlicerTestingData` release `SHA256` (content-addressed) | CC-BY-SA 4.0 |

Pinned source URL (SPEC section 7):

- https://github.com/Slicer/SlicerTestingData/releases/download/SHA256/4507b664690840abb6cb9af2d919377ffc4ef75b167cb6fd0f747befdb12e38e
  (source file `CT-chest.nrrd`, source SHA256 `4507b664690840abb6cb9af2d919377ffc4ef75b167cb6fd0f747befdb12e38e`)

`sample_ct.nrrd` is the source volume downsampled to 128x128x70 (all axes
<= 128, SPEC section 5 memory budget) and re-written as a raw NRRD by
`tools/convert_nrrd.py` at setup time; the committed file's own SHA256 is
recorded in `data/README.md` and SPEC section 7.

## Attribution (CC-BY-SA 4.0)

`sample_ct.nrrd` is derived from `CT-chest.nrrd`, task 06 (Lung) of the
Medical Segmentation Decathlon test set:

- Antonelli, M., Reinke, A., Bakas, S., et al. "The Medical Segmentation
  Decathlon." Nature Communications 13, 4128 (2022).
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-30695-9
- License: CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
- Indication of changes: downsampled to 128x128x70 and re-written as a raw
  NRRD by `tools/convert_nrrd.py` (this repository).
